<DocsLayout title="Rank & Rating" description="How Convocados rates players and prices a win: Elo, Glicko, teams, and the Season Rank redesign.">
  <h1>Rank &amp; Rating</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">One equation, four lessons, and the reason a win can pay nothing.</p>

  <p>
    These pages explain the maths behind Convocados' rankings and the product redesign
    built on it. The through-line: the failure was never a bad formula — it was asking
    <em>one</em> number to do <em>two</em> jobs.
  </p>

  <h2>Two numbers, two jobs</h2>
  <p>
    ADR 0031 separates the hidden Skill Rating from the visible Season Rank. They look
    similar and must not be crossed.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Skill Rating</th><th>Season Rank</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Job</td><td>Predict performance; balance teams</td><td>Make progress felt; give a goal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Audience</td><td>Organizer, matchmaking</td><td>Every player</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Visibility</td><td>Hidden (admin only)</td><td>Visible to members</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Horizon</td><td>Lifetime; never resets</td><td>Per Season; soft-resets</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Engine</td><td>Glicko-2 / OpenSkill</td><td>Transparent point payouts</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Failure to avoid</td><td>Unfair teams</td><td>"+0 after a win"</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

